<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore weekly mid-dist stocks down - TDB.</title>
<headline>Singapore weekly mid-dist stocks down - TDB.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's weekly middle distillate stocks were down for the first time since end May, falling by 1.331 million barrels to 10.744 million in the week ending July 2, Singapore's Trade Development Board (TDB) data showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>The following table shows the latest Singapore oil product stocks position, based on data from the TDB:</p>
<p>(figures in thousands of barrels)</p>
<p>		   Light		Middle</p>
<p>Wk ending   Distillates	Distillates     Residues</p>
<p>Jul 02	6,795 (+737)     10,744 (-1,331) 10,788 (-1,400)</p>
<p>Jun 25	6,058 (-47)	12,075 (+500)   12,188 (+480)</p>
<p>Jun 18	6,105 (-270)     11,575 (+339)   11,708 (+960)</p>
<p>Jun 11	6,375 (-381)     11,236 (+993)   10,748 (+436)</p>
<p>Jun 4	 6,756 (-94)	10,243 (-301)   10,312 (-465)</p>
<p>Middle distillates comprises jet, kerosene and gas oil.</p>
<p>Residues comprise high and low sulphur fuel oil, low sulphur waxy residue and straight-run atmospheric residue. Residues exclude bitumen.  </p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3080)</p>
